name w4-03-below-floor
timeout 420
time 1999-03-24T10:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W4, SORTIE 3 OF 10 - ALLIED FORCE 1999.
# THE SAME STRIKE FROM UNDER THE FLOOR - THE OTHER HALF OF THE TRADE.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w4-allied-force.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w4-01-floor.fbm - identical but for ONE fact, the ingress altitude (4,572 -> 1,200 m,
# spawn and both waypoints), and the callsign prefix.
#
# THE ANCHOR: the 15,000 ft floor was a COMMAND decision, taken because of heavy MANPADS and AAA [T3],
# and it was argued about for the whole 78 days because it cost accuracy against dispersed targets.
# W4's §Gaps says the floor "is this campaign's whole subject and today it is an arbitrary altitude";
# `C1` and `C23` closed on 2026-07-28 and this pair is where the argument becomes two numbers.
#
# WHY THIS FILE AND NOT A `wx` LINE. W4's spec §3 puts a mountain-valley strike in slot 3 and asks how
# much of the miss is the wind and how much the terrain-relative geometry. THAT QUESTION IS NOT
# ASKABLE IN THIS TREE and the campaign says so rather than dressing a straight line up as a valley:
# `C4` means no terrain masks anything, and `--elev const` means there is no valley at all - the
# ground is one plane. The wind half of it is measured, in full and with a sensitivity ladder, by
# sortie 02 and attribution A1. The slot went to the other side of the floor, which is the thing §2's
# contract calls "the thing the missions push against".
#
# 1,200 m is [SET]: it is below the ZU-23-2's 1,500 m ceiling and below the Strela-2M's 2,300 m one,
# i.e. inside BOTH short-range layers, which is what "under the floor" has to mean for the trade to
# be a trade. The cast, the aim point, the two `zone` cylinders and the timeout are 01's, unchanged.
#
# THE FOUR STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES: see w4-01-floor.fbm. Disclosure 1 bites hardest here - a 1,200 m
# ingress is exactly the profile real terrain would have masked, and this arena has none.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT DOES GOING UNDER THE FLOOR BUY, AND WHAT DOES IT COST?
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the expected verdict and it is NOT a failure - the
# striker survives and kills its target, and the run simply has nowhere else to go. Read
# `stores DELIVERY aimErrM` against 01's, then `zone_flak_s` against 01's 0.0 s, then every `site` and
# `gun` line the two short-range positions produced, then the closest approach of the SA-6's rounds.
# Do NOT read "it survived" as "it was safe".
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 858393e587dae283, exit 3): UNDER THE FLOOR THE BOMB IS NO BETTER AND THE
# AIRCRAFT IS INSIDE EVERYTHING.
#   the bomb          `aimErrM` **46.99 m** against 01's **41.09 m** - the low run is 5.9 m WORSE, and
#                     the campaign reports that rather than the result it expected. `predErrM` 49.91 m
#                     against 58.08 m, i.e. the COMPUTER is better low by 8.2 m and the DELIVERY is
#                     not: the release tick quantises the difference away. See 01's ladder
#   the short layer   `k3man` (Strela-2M) TRACKs at t=153.0 and **LAUNCHES twice** (t=161.9, 267.7);
#                     `k3flk` (ZU-23-2) TRACKs at t=164.0 and empties **40 of 40 rounds** in three
#                     bursts from t=172.3. In 01 both produced 0 TRACK and 0 LAUNCH. THE FLOOR IS AN
#                     ENVELOPE WALL AND 3,372 m OF ALTITUDE IS THE WHOLE OF IT
#   the zones         `zone_flak_s` = **347.3 s** against 01's 0.0 s; `zone_sambelt_s` = **0.0 s**
#                     against 01's 285.2 s. `objective avoid zone flak exposure 0` **UNMET** - the one
#                     objective in this campaign a route decision alone decides
#   the SAM layer     the 2K12 still reaches, and it reaches BETTER: 3 launches, and the two that flew
#                     pass the aircraft at **9.22 m and 13.57 m against an 8 m fuze**. In 01 the same
#                     battery fired the same three rounds and none came near. The low route is worse in
#                     BOTH currencies at once
#   THE HONEST SUMMARY: on this arena, under this catalogue, going below the floor buys NOTHING. Every
#   SAM row in `modules/ground/catalogue.md` reaches down to 100-450 m, so a low ingress leaves no
#   envelope and enters two more. What the real low ingress bought was TERRAIN, and terrain is `C4`.

zone flak 42.70000 20.98000 14000 0 3500
zone sambelt 42.70000 20.98000 14000 3500 8000

unit k3str
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 42.70000 20.60000 1200 90.0 450     # the ONE fact that differs from w4-01: 1,200 m
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.70000 21.10000 1200 450
  wp 42.70000 20.70000 1200 450
  objective kill unit k3tgt
  objective survive
  objective avoid zone flak

unit k3man
  module sa7
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.06000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 2

unit k3flk
  module zu23
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.09000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 40

unit k3sam
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 42.66000 20.98000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 3

unit k3tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.10000 ground 90.0 0
